ontentment, or satisfaction', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Angniryaraq', 'yDesc': "Tanqigcesnganani umyuam tungiinun ukutun, nunaniryuk, elluiyaraq, wall' assililuni", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Tanqigcesngananiumyuamtungiinunukutun', 'nunaniryuk', 'elluiyaraq', 'wall’assililuni'], 'resourceID': '3'}, '54': {'eTerm': 'Sadness', 'eDesc': 'A low emotional state characterized by feelings of sorrow, grief, or unhappiness', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Angniicaraq', 'yDesc': "Umyuaran ayuqucia aciqsigluni ukutun ilulliqsaraq, iluteqsaraq, wall' angniicaraq", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Umyuaranayuquciaaciqsigluniukutunilulliqsaraq', 'iluteqsaraq', 'wall’angniicaraq'], 'resourceID': '3'}, '55': {'eTerm': 'Anger', 'eDesc': 'An intense emotional response often associated with feelings of fear, displeasure, frustration, or offense', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Qenerrneq', 'yDesc': "Tuknilria umyuam ayuqucia an'aqluni alingaqami, assilinritaqami, makugtaqami, wall' umyuara nallaringanritaqan", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Tuknilriaumyuamayuquciaan’aqlunialingaqami', 'assilinritaqami', 'makugtaqami', 'wall’umyuaranallaringanritaqan'], 'resourceID': '3'}, '56': {'eTerm': 'Fear', 'eDesc': 'An emotional response to a perceived threat or danger, often accompanied by a sense of unease or anxiety. Can be based on real or imagined factors', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Alingun', 'yDesc': "Umyuam nallunairyaraa ellangaqan alingciraqatni wall' aarnarqellriim, amllerqunek tapengqeraqluni arenqianamek wall' umyuarniurutmek. Avalitait piciuyugngaluni wall' piciuvkenateng", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Umyuamnallunairyaraaellangaqanalingciraqatniwall’aarnarqellriim', 'amllerqunektapengqeraqluniarenqianamekwall’umyuarniurutmek.Avalitaitpiciuyugngaluniwall’piciuvkenateng'], 'resourceID': '3'}, '57': {'eTerm': 'Surprise', 'eDesc': 'A bried emotional state in response to something unexpected or suden', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Alangaaq', 'yDesc': "Umyuam ayuqliriqertellra umyuaqumanrilngurmek wall' alqunaqertellriamek", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Umyuamayuqliriqertellraumyuaqumanrilngurmekwall’alqunaqertellriamek'], 'resourceID': '3'}, '58': {'eTerm': 'Disgust', 'eDesc': 'A strong aversion or revulsion toward something unpleasant or offensive', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Cumaciyugyaraq', 'yDesc': "Cakneq assikevkenaku wall' quinakiluni camek assinrilngurmek wall' canganarqellriamek", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Cakneqassikevkenakuwall’quinakilunicamekassinrilngurmekwall’canganarqellriamek'], 'resourceID': '3'}, '59': {'eTerm': 'Contempt', 'eDesc': 'An internal rejection and/or judgement toward someone/something which we perceive as being below our standards', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': ' Arrsakiyaraq', 'yDesc': "Ilumikun/umyuamikun nekakluku cali/wall' pinarqutlirluku kina/ca tangvaumalria aciqsinruluku wangkutni", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Ilumikun/umyuamikunnekaklukucali/wall’pinarqutlirlukukina/catangvaumalriaaciqsinrulukuwangkutni'], 'resourceID': '3'}, '60': {'eTerm': 'Interest', 'eDesc': 'A state of curiousity, engagement, or attention toward something stimulating or captivating', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Paqnanaq', 'yDesc': "Paqnakluku, cumikluku, wall' murilkelluku ca iillanarqellria wall' tangvagyunaqluni", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Paqnakluku', 'cumikluku', 'wall’murilkellukucaiillanarqellriawall’tangvagyunaqluni'], 'resourceID': '3'}, '61': {'eTerm': 'Boredom', 'eDesc': 'A feeling of weariness or dissatisfaction resulting from a lack of interest or stimulation', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': "Nunaniryugpek'nani", 'yDesc': "Cayuumiinani wall' assilivkenani cucukenrilamiu wall' anglanakenrilamiu", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Cayuumiinaniwall’assilivkenanicucukenrilamiuwall’anglanakenrilamiu'], 'resourceID': '3'}, '62': {'eTerm': 'Love', 'eDesc': 'A deep affection and connection toward someone or something, often accompanied by care and concern ', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Kenka', 'yDesc': "Yugmun wall' camun cakneq assikiluni aipaqsunakluku-llu, aulukuurluku peng'garutekaqluku-llu", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Yugmunwall’camuncakneqassikiluniaipaqsunakluku-llu', 'aulukuurlukupeng’garutekaqluku-llu'], 'resourceID': '3'}, '63': {'eTerm': 'Jealousy', 'eDesc': 'A comples emotional state invloving feeling of envy, insecurity, or possessiveness', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Ciknakiyaraq', 'yDesc': "Capernarqellria umyuartuyaraq makutgun ayariluni, ellminek piyukevkenani, wall' cirlakluku", 'yNotes': ' ', 'speakers': ['Capernarqellriaumyuartuyaraqmakutgunayariluni', 'ellminekpiyukevkenani', 'wall’cirlakluku'], 'resourceID': '3'}, '64': {'eTerm': 'Guilt', 'eDesc': 'A sense of remorse or self-reproach resulting from a belief that one has done something wrong ', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Umyuarniuryaraq', 'yDesc': "Umyuarrluggluni wall' ellminek avalitekluni ukverngami alartellruniluni", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Umyuarrluggluniwall’ellminekavalitekluniukverngamialartellruniluni'], 'resourceID': '3'}, '65': {'eTerm': 'Shame', 'eDesc': 'A strong feeling of embarrassment or disgrace, often linked to a perceived failure or moral violation', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Kasngunaq', 'yDesc': "Tuknilria ayuquciq kasnguyugluni wall' umyuarrluggluni, piurteksaicukluni wall' narurciyukluni narurtarkaunrilngurmek", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Tuknilriaayuquciqkasnguyugluniwall’umyuarrluggluni', 'piurteksaicukluniwall’narurciyukluninarurtarkaunrilngurmek'], 'resourceID': '3'}, '66': {'eTerm': 'Embarassment', 'eDesc': 'A temporary state of self-consiousness or awkwardness resulting from social situations', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Takaryugyaraq', 'yDesc': 'Takaryugluni yuut avatiintellerkaminek', 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Takaryugluniyuutavatiintellerkaminek'], 'resourceID': '3'}, '67': {'eTerm': 'Confidence', 'eDesc': "A state of self-assurance and belief in one's abilities or judgements", 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Kemyunarqekiyaraq', 'yDesc': "Ellminek kemyukluni ukvekluku-llu piyugngallni wall' pillerkiuryugngallni", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Ellminekkemyukluniukvekluku-llupiyugngallniwall’pillerkiuryugngallni'], 'resourceID': '3'}, '68': {'eTerm': 'Pride', 'eDesc': 'A positive emotional state associated with a sense of accomplishment or satisfaction', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Ukveraitnaq', 'yDesc': "Elluatuuluni umyuarturyaraq qaqicillerminek wall' cupumanaqluni", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Elluatuuluniumyuarturyaraqqaqicillerminekwall’cupumanaqluni'], 'resourceID': '3'}, '69': {'eTerm': 'Relaxation', 'eDesc': 'A calm and unstrained mental state often associated with a sense of ease or transquility', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Qinuitneq', 'yDesc': "Umyuaq menuinani cagnerpegnani ayuqluni elluilriatun wall' qinuinani", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Umyuaqmenuinanicagnerpegnaniayuqlunielluilriatunwall’qinuinani'], 'resourceID': '3'}, '70': {'eTerm': 'Stress', 'eDesc': 'A state of mental or emotional strain resulting from challenging or adverse situations', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Umyuarrlugnaq', 'yDesc': "Cakviurnarqellriit wall' alingnarqellriit iqungqertuq umyuam nangteqellranek wall' caknaanarqellranek", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ["Cakviurnarqellriitwall'alingnarqellriitiqungqertuqumyuamnangteqellranekwall'caknaanarqellranek"], 'resourceID': '3'}, '71': {'eTerm': 'Anxiety', 'eDesc': 'A heightened state of worry, apprehension, or unease often accompanied by physical symptoms', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Umyuarniurun', 'yDesc': "Umyuarniussiyaagluni, ancurturluni, wall' arenqiayugluni tapeqluki temem aviranarqutai", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Umyuarniussiyaagluni', 'ancurturluni', 'wall’arenqiayuglunitapeqlukitememaviranarqutai'], 'resourceID': '3'}, '72': {'eTerm': 'Depression', 'eDesc': 'A persistent and pervasive low mood characterized by feeling of sadness, hopelessness, and loss of interest', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Umyuiqsaraq Aliayugpagluni', 'yDesc': 'Taqsuunani cali ciuniurumanrilnguq umyuam ayuqucia aliayugluni kesianek, manimaluteng aliayugluni, neryuniurutaunani, ilagaucuumiirulluni-llu.', 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Taqsuunanicaliciuniurumanrilnguqumyuamayuquciaaliayuglunikesianek', 'manimalutengaliayugluni', 'neryuniurutaunani', 'ilagaucuumiirulluni-llu.'], 'resourceID': '3'}, '73': {'eTerm': 'Frustration', 'eDesc': 'A state of dissatisfaction and irritation resulting from obstacles or unmet desires ', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Makugcaraq', 'yDesc': "Assilivkenani eqnayugluni-llu canek wall' piyullni unakeksailamiki", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Assilivkenanieqnayugluni-llucanekwall’piyullniunakeksailamiki'], 'resourceID': '3'}, '74': {'eTerm': 'Euphoria', 'eDesc': 'An intense and elevated mood characterized by feelings of extreme happiness and excitement ', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Angniq', 'yDesc': 'Tukniluni quyigluni-llu ayuquciq angnipiarluni qiilerrluni-llu', 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Tukniluniquyigluni-lluayuquciqangnipiarluniqiilerrluni-llu'], 'resourceID': '3'}, '75': {'eTerm': 'Apathy', 'eDesc': 'A lack of interest, enthusiasm, or motivation toward activities or life in general ', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Cayuumiitelleq', 'yDesc': "Cayuumiinani, tengruvkenani, wall' ilagaucuumiinani calrianun wall' yuucimun.", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Cayuumiinani', 'tengruvkenani', 'wall’ilagaucuumiinanicalrianunwall’yuucimun.'], 'resourceID': '3'}, '76': {'eTerm': 'Nostalgia', 'eDesc': 'A sentimental longing or affectionate remembrance of the past', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Yuarnayugyaraq', 'yDesc': "Yuarnakluku wall' umyuaqutkegciluku kinguneq.", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Yuarnaklukuwall’umyuaqutkegcilukukinguneq.'], 'resourceID': '3'}, '77': {'eTerm': 'Helpless', 'eDesc': 'Lacking the ability or power to take action or make change; feeling unable to help oneself', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Nanikuayaraq', 'yDesc': "Cacetuvkenani wall' qaillun pisciiganani wall' cimirciiganani; ellminek ikayurciigalnganani. ", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Cacetuvkenaniwall’qaillunpisciigananiwall’cimirciiganani;ellminekikayurciigalnganani.'], 'resourceID': '3'}, '78': {'eTerm': 'Trapped', 'eDesc': 'Unable to escape from a situation or place; feeling confined or restricted, with limited options for movement or action', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Kalivqinalriit', 'yDesc': "Ayagciiganani callminek wall' uitaviminek; itengqanganani wall' natvarciigalnganani, ayagvigkaa wall' callra ikgenani.", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Ayagciigananicallminekwall’uitaviminek;itengqangananiwall’natvarciigalnganani', 'ayagvigkaawall’callraikgenani.'], 'resourceID': '3'}, '79': {'eTerm': 'Ambivalence', 'eDesc': 'Experiencing mixed or conflicting emotions or attitutes toward a particular situation, person, or decision, making it challenging to choose or commit to a specific course of action', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Uunguciicaraq', 'yDesc': "Uunguciinani wall' nalirruggluni callminek, yugmek, wall' pillerkaminek, caperrnariluku cucukillerkaq wall' caqatallerminek.", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Uunguciinaniwall’nalirrugglunicallminek', 'yugmek', 'wall’pillerkaminek', 'caperrnarilukucucukillerkaqwall’caqatallerminek.'], 'resourceID': '4'}, '80': {'eTerm': 'Openness', 'eDesc': 'Willing to accept and consider new ideas, perspectives, or experiences', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Allakaukinailnguq', 'yDesc': "Ciuniuriyugngaluni umyuartuuteksugngaluki-llu nutarat pillerkat, qaillun tangvaumallrit, wall' callrit.", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Ciuniuriyugngaluniumyuartuuteksugngaluki-llunutaratpillerkat', 'qailluntangvaumallrit', 'wall’callrit.'], 'resourceID': '4'}, '81': {'eTerm': 'Hesitation', 'eDesc': 'A temporary pause or delay in decision-making or action, often stemming fom uncertainty, doubt, or lack of confidence in choosing the best course of option', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Nasperturyaraq', 'yDesc': "Pillerkiuringnaqkuni wall' caqataquni arulaiqerluni wall' qariqerrluni, ancurtuami, asguranakngamiu, wall' ellminek kemyukenrilami cucukinritnayukluni assinranek.", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Pillerkiuringnaqkuniwall’caqataquniarulaiqerluniwall’qariqerrluni', 'ancurtuami', 'asguranakngamiu', 'wall’ellminekkemyukenrilamicucukinritnayukluniassinranek.'], 'resourceID': '4'}, '82': {'eTerm': 'Coping Strategies', 'eDesc': 'Ways people deal with and manage stress, challenges or difficult emotions. These can include various actions, thoughts, or behaviors that help people navigate tough situations', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Qaillun Auluksaurcugngariyaraq', 'yDesc': "Yuut qaillun aulukitullrat umyuamun arcarillret, cakviurutet, wall' caperrnarqellriit umyuarniurutet.  Ilakluki ayuqenrilnguut callrit, umyuartuutet, wall' yuut ikayuutait qaillun ayagturallerkaatnun cakviungermeng.", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Yuutqaillunaulukitullratumyuamunarcarillret', 'cakviurutet', 'wall’caperrnarqellriitumyuarniurutet.Ilaklukiayuqenrilnguutcallrit', 'umyuartuutet', 'wall’yuutikayuutaitqaillunayagturallerkaatnuncakviungermeng.'], 'resourceID': '5'}, '83': {'eTerm': 'Healing', 'eDesc': 'The process of becoming healthy and whole again. It often involves recovery and improvement after a period of illness, trauma, or distress. ', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Mamyaraq', 'yDesc': "Calricaraq tamalkuurcaraq-llu.  Aturnarqelartuq utumariyaraq assiriinallerkaq-llu naulluurraarluni, umyuaq akngirterrarcelluku, wall' arenqialliurraarcelluku.", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Calricaraqtamalkuurcaraq-llu.Aturnarqelartuqutumariyaraqassiriinallerkaq-llunaulluurraarluni', 'umyuaqakngirterrarcelluku', 'wall’arenqialliurraarcelluku.'], 'resourceID': '5'}, '84': {'eTerm': 'Support', 'eDesc': 'Assistance, encouragement, or comfort provided by others, such as friends, family, or a community. Support can be emotional, practical, or both', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Cingumayaraq', 'yDesc': "Allat ikayurluku, cingumaluku, wall' qarulluku, ukutun yugnikekngat, ilait, wall' nunalgutaita.  Cingumayugngauq umyuarakun, aipaqluku, wall' tamarkegenka.", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Allatikayurluku', 'cingumaluku', 'wall’qarulluku', 'ukutunyugnikekngat', 'ilait', 'wall’nunalgutaita.Cingumayugngauqumyuarakun', 'aipaqluku', 'wall’tamarkegenka.'], 'resourceID': '5'}, '85': {'eTerm': 'Harm Reduction', 'eDesc': 'An approach focused on reducing  the risks of certain behaviors or conditions, without completely stopping all the behaviors themselves. Small changes over time can have major long-term effects.', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Ikgelicarluku Akngirun', 'yDesc': "Ikeglingnaqluki aarnarqellriit ayuqucii wall' uitallra, tau͡gaam tamalkuita arulaircetevkenaki aarnarqellriit atuqekngai. Ikgenaki cimiryarait cakviurnarqelartut ak'anun.", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Ikeglingnaqlukiaarnarqellriitayuquciiwall’uitallra', 'tau͡gaamtamalkuitaarulaircetevkenakiaarnarqellriitatuqekngai.Ikgenakicimiryaraitcakviurnarqelartutak’anun.'], 'resourceID': '5'}, '86': {'eTerm': 'Habits', 'eDesc': 'Consistent, often unconscious, behaviors that people develop throughout their lives. Habits can be both positive and negative, influencing daily routines and lifestyle choices', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Piuryarat', 'yDesc': "Cimiyuinateng, amllerqunek elpeksuunaku, piciryarait yuut piciryaraksagutellrit yuucimegni. Piciryarat assiryugngaut wall' assiicugngaut, agtuumaluki cayarait yuuyarait-llu.", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Cimiyuinateng', 'amllerqunekelpeksuunaku', 'piciryaraityuutpiciryaraksagutellrityuucimegni.Piciryaratassiryugngautwall’assiicugngaut', 'agtuumalukicayaraityuuyarait-llu.'], 'resourceID': '5'}, '87': {'eTerm': 'Curable', 'eDesc': "When an illness is curable, it means that there is a treatment or intervention that can completely get rid of the illness. Imagine it like fixing a problem so that it goes away permanently, like taking antibiotics for a bacterial infection, once the treatment is successful, the illness is gone, and you don't have to worry about it coming back.", 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Mamyugngalria', 'yDesc': "Naulluun mamyugngalriarukuni, kangingqerciquq yuungcaryugngaluni wall' naulluun arulaivkangnaqluku catairutlerkaanun tamalkuan. Tangrruarluku kitugillerkaa arenqiallugutem ayagniartuq taqluni, iinrukitellriatun pupik pitekluku. Iinruk calikuni naulluun catairuciiquq, peng'garnairulluni-llu tainqigtellerkaanek.", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Naulluunmamyugngalriarukuni', 'kangingqerciquqyuungcaryugngaluniwall’naulluunarulaivkangnaqlukucatairutlerkaanuntamalkuan.Tangrruarlukukitugillerkaaarenqiallugutemayagniartuqtaqluni', 'iinrukitellriatunpupikpitekluku.Iinrukcalikuninaulluuncatairuciiquq', 'peng’garnairulluni-llutainqigtellerkaanek.'], 'resourceID': '5'}, '88': {'eTerm': 'Treatable', 'eDesc': 'When an illness is treatable, it means that there are ways to manage or alleviate the symptoms of the illness. But it may not be possible to get rid of it completely or permanently.  Think of it like managing a chronic condition, such as diabetes. With ongoing treatment and lifestyle adjustments, you can control the symptoms and live a healthy life, but the condition might not go away entirely', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Assiriyugngalria', 'yDesc': "Naulluun assiriyugngalria, auluksugngaciquq wall' ikegliyugngaciquq tamana naulluun, tau͡gaam tamarmi catairucesciigaciiqngatuq. Umyuaqluku auluknarqellra ak'anun naulluun, saarralissiyaalriatun auk tequq-llu. Yuungcarturaquni cali yuuciq kitugareskuni, auluknarqelarciquq cali yuuluaqernaqluni, tau͡gaam tauna naulluun tamarmi assiringaituq", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Naulluunassiriyugngalria', 'auluksugngaciquqwall’ikegliyugngaciquqtamananaulluun', 'tau͡gaamtamarmicatairucesciigaciiqngatuq.Umyuaqlukuauluknarqellraak’anunnaulluun', 'saarralissiyaalriatunauktequq-llu.Yuungcarturaqunicaliyuuciqkitugareskuni', 'auluknarqelarciquqcaliyuuluaqernaqluni', 'tau͡gaamtaunanaulluuntamarmiassiringaituq'], 'resourceID': '5'}, '89': {'eTerm': 'Informal Supports', 'eDesc': 'Personal assistance and help that people receive from friends, family, or social networks', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Allat Cingumastet', 'yDesc': "Yuk ikayurcelluni cali ikayungqerrluni yugnikek'ngaminek, ilaminek, wall' allanek ikayuritulinek.", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ["Yukikayurcellunicaliikayungqerrluniyugnikek'ngaminek", 'ilaminek', 'wall’allanekikayuritulinek.'], 'resourceID': '6'}, '90': {'eTerm': 'Community Resources', 'eDesc': 'Services, organizations, or facilities available within a community that provide support, assistance, or information to residents. These resources can include healthcare services, community centers, educational programs, and more. ', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Nunaitni Ikayungcarviit', 'yDesc': "Kevgiurutet, quyungqalriit ikayurtet, wall' caliviit paivngalriit nunani cingumasteńguluteng, ikayuriluteng, wall' nallunairiluteng yugnun. Makut ikayuutet ilangqerrsugngaut calricaram kevgiuriyaraanek, nunat quyurrvigkaatnek, elitnauryaranek, allanek-llu.", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Kevgiurutet', 'quyungqalriitikayurtet', 'wall’caliviitpaivngalriitnunanicingumasteńguluteng', 'ikayuriluteng', 'wall’nallunairilutengyugnun.Makutikayuutetilangqerrsugngautcalricaramkevgiuriyaraanek', 'nunatquyurrvigkaatnek', 'elitnauryaranek', 'allanek-llu.'], 'resourceID': '6'}, '91': {'eTerm': 'Protective Factors', 'eDesc': "Parts of a person's life or environment that increase their resilience and help them manage stress and difficulties. They contribute to a person's well-being and can act as a buffer against stressors.", 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Qaunqiyarat', 'yDesc': "Yuucim iliin wall' avatiin quyigikanircet'laraa pinirikanircelluku ikayurluku-llu aulukluku umyuarniurun caperrnarqellriit-llu. Ikayuutelartut yuum calricaraanun cayailkucilriatun-llu ayuqluku umyuarniurutkanun.", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ["Yuucimiliinwall’avatiinquyigikanircet'laraapinirikanircellukuikayurluku-lluauluklukuumyuarniuruncaperrnarqellriit-llu.Ikayuutelartutyuumcalricaraanuncayailkucilriatun-lluayuqlukuumyuarniurutkanun."], 'resourceID': '6'}, '92': {'eTerm': 'Risk Factors', 'eDesc': "Parts of a person's life that increase the likelihood of negative outcomes or problems", 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Aarnarqellriit', 'yDesc': "Yuum yuucian iliin arcariluki assinrilnguut wall' arenqiallugutait.", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Yuumyuucianiliinarcarilukiassinrilnguutwall’arenqiallugutait.'], 'resourceID': '6'}, '93': {'eTerm': 'Treatment Plan', 'eDesc': "A detailed and structure strategy developed by healthcare professionals to address an individual's specific health or behavioral issues. It outlines the intended interventions, therapeutic approaches, and goals to achieve the desired outcomes", 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Yuungcallerkam Pillerkiuraa', 'yDesc': "Iinrivigmi calistet ayagnillrit apertuumanqegcaaraumalria atuyunarqellria-llu pillerkiuraq caliaqsugluku yuum calricaraa wall' arenqiallugutii. Pillerkiulartuq ikayullerkaanek, qaillun assiringcallerkaanek, egmirutekaanek-llu piyuutiin unakellerkaanek.", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Iinrivigmicalistetayagnillritapertuumanqegcaaraumalriaatuyunarqellria-llupillerkiuraqcaliaqsuglukuyuumcalricaraawall’arenqiallugutii.Pillerkiulartuqikayullerkaanek', 'qaillunassiringcallerkaanek', 'egmirutekaanek-llupiyuutiinunakellerkaanek.'], 'resourceID': '7'}, '94': {'eTerm': 'Goals', 'eDesc': 'Broad, overarching statements that describe the desired results or changes a person aims to achieve. In the context of a treatment plan, goals provide a general direction for progress and improvement', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Egmirutet', 'yDesc': "Qanerniarutet aperturiluteng iqukanek wall' cimirluki yuum piukekngai. Assirillerkam pillerkiuraani, egmirutekiulartut assirillerkam tungiinun cali utumarillerkamun.", 'yNotes': 'Egmirutet?', 'speakers': ['Qanerniarutetaperturilutengiqukanekwall’cimirlukiyuumpiukekngai.Assirillerkampillerkiuraani', 'egmirutekiulartutassirillerkamtungiinuncaliutumarillerkamun.'], 'resourceID': '7'}, '95': {'eTerm': 'Objective', 'eDesc': 'Specific, measurable, and time-bound steps or actions designed to achieve the broader goals outlined in a treatment plan. Objectives break down the goals into smaller, manageable components, making it easier to track progress and success.', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Picirkiurun', 'yDesc': "Apertuumanqegcaarluni, cuqcugngaluku, cali apertuutet taqlerkiurangqerrluteng wall' egmirutekait atuyunaqluteng yungcaryaraan pillerkiuraini.  Egmirutekat picirkiurutetgun atuyunarilartut ikeglillritgun, auluksunarillritgun, qacignarivkarluki cuqtellerkait assiriinaryaramun cali elluarillerkamun.", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Apertuumanqegcaarluni', 'cuqcugngaluku', 'caliapertuutettaqlerkiurangqerrlutengwall’egmirutekaitatuyunaqlutengyungcaryaraanpillerkiuraini.Egmirutekatpicirkiurutetgunatuyunarilartutikeglillritgun', 'auluksunarillritgun', 'qacignarivkarlukicuqtellerkaitassiriinaryaramuncalielluarillerkamun.'], 'resourceID': '7'}, '96': {'eTerm': 'Informed Consent', 'eDesc': 'Autonomy is closely tied to the concept of informed consent. Before any medical procedure or treatment, healthcare providers should provide patients with any available information about the types of help they are suggesting, including potential risks, benefits, and alternatives. ', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Nallunrirceciyaraq', 'yDesc': "Ellminek ataniuryaram ayuqeqapigta nallunrirceciyaraq.  Iinrivigmi cavailgatgu wall' yuungcarpailgatgu, calricariurtet nallunaircetarkaugait yuungcarvigtellriit nallunaircelluki ayuqenrilngurnek ikayuutekaitnek, ilaluki aarnarqutaitnek, ikayuutekaitnek, allanek-llu piyugngallritnek. ", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Ellminekataniuryaramayuqeqapigtanallunrirceciyaraq.Iinrivigmicavailgatguwall’yuungcarpailgatgu', 'calricariurtetnallunaircetarkaugaityuungcarvigtellriitnallunaircellukiayuqenrilngurnekikayuutekaitnek', 'ilalukiaarnarqutaitnek', 'ikayuutekaitnek', 'allanek-llupiyugngallritnek.'], 'resourceID': '8'}, '97': {'eTerm': 'Respecting Preferences', 'eDesc': 'Healthcare professionals should respect and consider the individual preferences and values of their patients. They must recognize that people may have diverse cultural, religious, or personal beliefs that influence their healthcare decisions.', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Qigcikluki Piyuutait', 'yDesc': "Calricariurtet qigcikarkaugait cali umyuartuutekluki iinrivigtellriit piyuutait arcaqakekngait-llu.  Elitaqumaarkaugait yuut ayuqenrilngurnek yuuyarangqellrit, agayumaciit, wall' ukverutait calricaram pillerkiuryaraan tungiinun. ", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Calricariurtetqigcikarkaugaitcaliumyuartuuteklukiiinrivigtellriitpiyuutaitarcaqakekngait-llu.Elitaqumaarkaugaityuutayuqenrilngurnekyuuyarangqellrit', 'agayumaciit', 'wall’ukverutaitcalricarampillerkiuryaraantungiinun.'], 'resourceID': '8'}, '98': {'eTerm': 'Shared Decision-Making', 'eDesc': 'Autonomy encourages providers to work together with their patients for all decision making rather than choosing what should be done about any identified problems alone. ', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Ikayuqulluteng Pillerkiuriyaraq', 'yDesc': "Ellminek ataniuriyaram cingumalarai calricariurtet calillgutkesqumaluki iinrivigtellriit ilakluki pillerkiurillerkait kiingan arenqiallugutait auluklerkai tangvagpek'naku. ", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ["Ellminekataniuriyaramcingumalaraicalricariurtetcalillgutkesqumalukiiinrivigtellriitilaklukipillerkiurillerkaitkiinganarenqiallugutaitauluklerkaitangvagpek'naku."], 'resourceID': '8'}, '99': {'eTerm': 'Confidentiality', 'eDesc': 'Respecting autonomy includes ensuring the confidentiality of patient information. Patients should feel confident that their personal health information will be kept private unless they give clear permission for it to be used in specific ways.', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Qalarutkumaarkaunrilnguut', 'yDesc': 'Qigcikiyaraq ellminek ataniuriyaramek ilangqertuq qalarutkarkaunritellranek iinrivigtellriim nallunairutainek.  Iinrivigtellriit kemyunakarkaugait calricaraata nallunairutait qanrutkumaarkaunritellritnek apterraarpailgan atuusqelluku qaillun.', 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Qigcikiyaraqellminekataniuriyaramekilangqertuqqalarutkarkaunritellranekiinrivigtellriimnallunairutainek.Iinrivigtellriitkemyunakarkaugaitcalricaraatanallunairutaitqanrutkumaarkaunritellritnekapterraarpailganatuusqellukuqaillun.'], 'resourceID': '8'}, '100': {'eTerm': 'Refusal of Treatment', 'eDesc': 'Patients have the right to refuse medical treatment, even if healthcare providers believe it is in their best interest. This refusal should be respected, and alternative options or consequences should be discussed.', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Yuungcaasqumanritlerkaq', 'yDesc': "Iinrivigtellriit piyunarqucingqertut ciuniunricugngaluki yuungcaryarateng, calricariurtet ukvengraatki assirniluku taumun. Ciuniurinritleq qigcikumaarkauguq, cali qalarutkarkaugut allaggun yuungcallerkamek wall' qaillun piciqellranek ciuniurumanrilkan yuungcarrsuutekaa.   ", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Iinrivigtellriitpiyunarqucingqertutciuniunricugngalukiyuungcaryarateng', 'calricariurtetukvengraatkiassirnilukutaumun.Ciuniurinritleqqigcikumaarkauguq', 'caliqalarutkarkaugutallaggunyuungcallerkamekwall’qaillunpiciqellranekciuniurumanrilkanyuungcarrsuutekaa.'], 'resourceID': '8'}, '101': {'eTerm': 'Cultural Competence', 'eDesc': 'Autonomy recognizes the importance of cultural competence in healthcare. Healthcare providers should be sensitive to the cultural backgrounds of their patients and adapt their approach to treatment accordingly. ', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Yuuyaram Atuuyugngallra', 'yDesc': 'Ellminek ataniuryaram elitaqumaa arcaqaucia yuuyaraq calricarami.  Calricariurtet elpekumarkaugait yuuyaraat iinrivigtellriit cali yungcarillermeggnun aturluki pinarqekan.', 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Ellminekataniuryaramelitaqumaaarcaqauciayuuyaraqcalricarami.Calricariurtetelpekumarkaugaityuuyaraatiinrivigtellriitcaliyungcarillermeggnunaturlukipinarqekan.'], 'resourceID': '8'}, '102': {'eTerm': 'Guardianship and Incapacity', 'eDesc': "In cases where a person lacks the capacity to make decisions for themselves, autonomy may involve appointing a legal guardian for them. Even in these situations, efforts should be made to understand and consider the individual's wishes and values.", 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Aulukiyaraq cali Casciigalnguq', 'yDesc': "Kina yuk pillerkiurciigalkan ellminek, ataniuryaram ellminek ilaksugngaa qanercetaarvigkun aulukestekilluku tauna.  Wat'nangraan, taringnarqerkauguq cali umyuaqluku yuum piyuutii arcaqakekngai-llu.", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Kinayukpillerkiurciigalkanellminek', 'ataniuryaramellminekilaksugngaaqanercetaarvigkunaulukestekillukutauna.Wat’nangraan', 'taringnarqerkauguqcaliumyuaqlukuyuumpiyuutiiarcaqakekngai-llu.'], 'resourceID': '8'}, '103': {'eTerm': 'Educating and Empowering Patients', 'eDesc': 'Autonomy involves empowering patients with information and resources to actively participate in their healthcare decisions. This includes providing education about their medical conditions, treatment options, and self-management strategies.', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Elicungcarluki Atanrurtelluki Inrivigtellriit', 'yDesc': 'Ellminek ataniuryaram ilakaa inrivigtellriit piyunarqucilirluki ilagaucugngallrit nallunairutnek ikayuutekanek-llu pillerkiurillratni calricaramegnek. Ilakluki elicungcarluki naulluutaitnek, yuungcarrsuutekaitnek, ellaitnek pillerkiuraita auluksaraitnek-llu.', 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Ellminekataniuryaramilakaainrivigtellriitpiyunarqucilirlukiilagaucugngallritnallunairutnekikayuutekanek-llupillerkiurillratnicalricaramegnek.Ilaklukielicungcarlukinaulluutaitnek', 'yuungcarrsuutekaitnek', 'ellaitnekpillerkiuraitaauluksaraitnek-llu.'], 'resourceID': '8'}, '104': {'eTerm': 'Precontemplation', 'eDesc': 'The person is not yet considering change. They may be unaware or in denial of a need for any change.', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Cimirngaicuklukuaq', 'yDesc': "Yuk umyuarturpek'nani cimillerkaminek.  Aipaagni tayima elpekenritaa wall' cimirnarqenricuklukuarluni. ", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ["Yukumyuarturpek'nanicimillerkaminek.Aipaagnitayimaelpekenritaawall’cimirnarqenricuklukuarluni."], 'resourceID': '9'}, '105': {'eTerm': 'Contemplation', 'eDesc': 'The person is aware of the need for change but is undecided. They may weigh the pros and cons of changing.', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Umyuartuuteksaraq', 'yDesc': 'Yuum elpekluku cimirnarqellni tau͡gken nalirruggluni.  Yuvriryugngaat cimillerkam assillra assinritellra-llu.', 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Yuumelpeklukucimirnarqellnitau͡gkennalirruggluni.Yuvriryugngaatcimillerkamassillraassinritellra-llu.'], 'resourceID': '9'}, '106': {'eTerm': 'Preparation', 'eDesc': 'The person has decided to make a change. They may begin planning and taking small steps toward change.', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Upcaraq', 'yDesc': 'Yuk umyuangellruuq cimiryugluni. Ayagniriluni pillerkiuramek cimirnaluni cukaunani-llu ayagniqcaarluni cimillerkaminun.  ', 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Yukumyuangellruuqcimiryugluni.Ayagnirilunipillerkiuramekcimirnalunicukaunani-lluayagniqcaarlunicimillerkaminun.'], 'resourceID': '9'}, '107': {'eTerm': 'Action', 'eDesc': 'The person actively engages in behaviors to make the change they want. This stage involves the most visible and noticeable changes in behavior.', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Egmirulluku/Ayagnirluku', 'yDesc': 'Yuum ayuqucini egmirulluku cimingnaqluni ayuqsullerminun.  Una cimiryaraq tangerrnarqellriaruuq elitaqnaqluteng-llu cimirturallra ayuquciaggun.', 'yNotes': 'ayuquciakun? ayuquciatgun?', 'speakers': ['Yuumayuquciniegmirullukucimingnaqluniayuqsullerminun.Unacimiryaraqtangerrnarqellriaruuqelitaqnaqluteng-llucimirturallraayuquciaggun.'], 'resourceID': '9'}, '108': {'eTerm': 'Maintenance', 'eDesc': 'The person works to keep the changes made during the action stage. This stage involves preventing relapse and consolidating gains.', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Aulukuuryaraq', 'yDesc': "Yuum caliaquurluku cimirturallni cimirtuuryaram nalliini. Mat'um cimirtuuryaram caliaqaa ataam ayuqelallmitun pinritengnaqsaraq cali elluatmun ayangnaquurluni.", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Yuumcaliaquurlukucimirturallnicimirtuuryaramnalliini.Mat’umcimirtuuryaramcaliaqaaataamayuqelallmitunpinritengnaqsaraqcalielluatmunayangnaquurluni.'], 'resourceID': '9'}, '109': {'eTerm': 'Credentials and Experience', 'eDesc': 'What is your educational background and professional training? How long have you been practicing therapy? Do you have experience working with [specific concerns or populations]?', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Piciutassiillerkaa Calillra-llu', 'yDesc': "Canek elitnaullrusit cali elicungcallrusit? Qaillun taktalriamek calillrurcit umyualiurteńguluten? Ciungani-qaa caliaqelallruaten [aperturiluten arenqiallugutnek wall' amllertaciit]?", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Canekelitnaullrusitcalielicungcallrusit?Qailluntaktalriamekcalillrurcitumyualiurteńguluten?Ciungani-qaacaliaqelallruaten[aperturilutenarenqiallugutnekwall’amllertaciit]?'], 'resourceID': '10'}, '110': {'eTerm': 'Therapeutic Approach', 'eDesc': 'What therapeutic approach or model do you primarily use? How do you tailor your approach to the needs of individual clients? Can you explain how you typically work with clients?', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Assiringnaqsaraam Ayagyaraa', 'yDesc': "Canek assiringcarrsuutnek wall' kitugutnek aturpallularcit? Qaillun atuyunarilarciki assiringcaryaraten piyuutaitnun ikayungnaqkevnun? Nalqigcugngaan-qaa qaillun ikayuringnaq'lallerpenek yugnun?", 'yNotes': 'assiringnaqsaram? assiringnaqsaraan?', 'speakers': ["Canekassiringcarrsuutnekwall’kitugutnekaturpallularcit?Qaillunatuyunarilarcikiassiringcaryaratenpiyuutaitnunikayungnaqkevnun?Nalqigcugngaan-qaaqaillunikayuringnaq'lallerpenekyugnun?"], 'resourceID': '10'}, '111': {'eTerm': 'Specialization', 'eDesc': 'Do you have experience in dealing with issues similar to mine? Are there particular areas or specialties you focus on in your practice?', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Caliarem Cumigutai', 'yDesc': 'Aulukillruuten-qaa arenqiallugutema ayuqiinek ciungani? Canek elisngakngavnek cumigutengqercit caliavni?', 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Aulukillruuten-qaaarenqiallugutemaayuqiinekciungani?Canekelisngakngavnekcumigutengqercitcaliavni?'], 'resourceID': '10'}, '112': {'eTerm': 'Logistics', 'eDesc': 'What are your fees, and do you accept insurance? What is your cancellation policy? How often are sessions scheduled, and what is the typical duration?', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Caliarem Ayagyaraa/Eglercaraa', 'yDesc': "Caugat akilitarkaci, insurance-aakun akilicugngauq? Taq'iyaram alerquutai caugat? Qavcirqunek quyurtelartat, cauga-llu taktacia?", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Caugatakilitarkaci', "insurance-aakunakilicugngauq?Taq'iyaramalerquutaicaugat?Qavcirqunekquyurtelartat", 'cauga-llutaktacia?'], 'resourceID': '10'}, '113': {'eTerm': 'Collaboration', 'eDesc': 'How do you collaborate with clients in developing treatment plans? Can we discuss and agree on the goals and expectations of therapy together?', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Calillguteksaraq', 'yDesc': "Qaillun calillgutek'larciki kevgiuqek'ngat ayagnirilluki assiringcaryaramek? Assiringcaryaram-qaa egmirutekai neryuniurutkai-llu qanaateksugngaarpuk umyuallguteklunuk?", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ["Qailluncalillgutek'larcikikevgiuqek'ngatayagnirillukiassiringcaryaramek?Assiringcaryaram-qaaegmirutekaineryuniurutkai-lluqanaateksugngaarpukumyuallguteklunuk?"], 'resourceID': '10'}, '114': {'eTerm': 'Feedback and Progress', 'eDesc': 'How do you gather feedback on the effectiveness of our sessions? What is your approach if I feel that therapy is not working for me?', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Nallunairiyaraq Ayagturyaraq-llu', 'yDesc': 'Quyurcaramnuk elluatuucian tungiinun qaillun quyurcilarcit nallunairanek? Umyualiuryaraq calinritnikumku qaillun aulukciqsiu?', 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Quyurcaramnukelluatuuciantungiinunqaillunquyurcilarcitnallunairanek?Umyualiuryaraqcalinritnikumkuqaillunaulukciqsiu?'], 'resourceID': '10'}, '115': {'eTerm': 'Crisis or Emergency Procedures', 'eDesc': 'What is your protocol for handling emergencies or crises? How can I reach you in case of an urgent situation?', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': "Pinarqeqapiaralria wall' Piqatararpek'naku Aulukunarqellriim Maligtaquarkait", 'yDesc': "Caugat auluksarai piqatarraarpek'naku auluknarqellriit wall' pinarqeqapiarluteng arenqiallugtellriit? Qaillun unaksugngaciqsia elpet arenqiallugeskuma pinarqeqapiaralriamek?", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ["Caugatauluksaraipiqatarraarpek'nakuauluknarqellriitwall’pinarqeqapiarlutengarenqiallugtellriit?Qaillununaksugngaciqsiaelpetarenqiallugeskumapinarqeqapiaralriamek?"], 'resourceID': '10'}, '116': {'eTerm': 'Communication and Boundaries', 'eDesc': 'How do you handle communication between sessions? What are your policies on confidentiality and privacy? Are there any limits to confidentiality that I should be aware of?', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Qalaruciyaraq/Nallunairiyaraq Qalaruteksukngakait-llu', 'yDesc': "Qaillun auluk'larciu qalaruciyaraq/nallunairiyaraq quyurtellerkat akuliitni? Caugat qalarutkenricaram qanrutkenricaram alerquutai? Qalarutkenricaraq-qaa iqungqertuq nallunritarkamnek?", 'yNotes': 'qalaruteksugngakait? qalruteksukekengakait?', 'speakers': ["Qaillunauluk'larciuqalaruciyaraq/nallunairiyaraqquyurtellerkatakuliitni?Caugatqalarutkenricaramqanrutkenricaramalerquutai?Qalarutkenricaraq-qaaiqungqertuqnallunritarkamnek?"], 'resourceID': '10'}, '117': {'eTerm': 'Goals and Expectations', 'eDesc': 'How do you approach goal setting in therapy? What can I expect from the therapeutic process, and how will progress be measured? How do you involve clients in the treatment planning process?', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Egmirutet cali Neryuniurutet', 'yDesc': "Qaillun caliaqelarciki egmiruciyaraq assiringcaraqata? Camek neryuniurucetangqerta assiringcaryarami, qaillun-llu assiriinallra cuqcimalarta? Qaillun kevgiurumalriit ilagaucet'larcetki assiringcaryaramek pillerkiuriaqavci?", 'yNotes': 'egmirutet?', 'speakers': ['Qailluncaliaqelarcikiegmiruciyaraqassiringcaraqata?Camekneryuniurucetangqertaassiringcaryarami', "qaillun-lluassiriinallracuqcimalarta?Qaillunkevgiurumalriitilagaucet'larcetkiassiringcaryaramekpillerkiuriaqavci?"], 'resourceID': '10'}, '118': {'eTerm': 'Cultural Competence', 'eDesc': 'How do you approach cultural competence and diversity in your practice? Have you worked with clients from diverse backgrounds, and how do you ensure sensitivity?', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Yuuyaram Elluatuuyaraa', 'yDesc': 'Qaillun atularciki yuuyarat elluatuuyarat ayuqenriluciat-llu caliarpeni? Kevgiurillruuten-qaa ayuqenrilngurnek yuuyaralegnek, qaillun-llu naklegtallren manilarciu?', 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Qaillunatularcikiyuuyaratelluatuuyaratayuqenriluciat-llucaliarpeni?Kevgiurillruuten-qaaayuqenrilngurnekyuuyaralegnek', 'qaillun-llunaklegtallrenmanilarciu?'], 'resourceID': '10'}, '119': {'eTerm': 'Client Involvement', 'eDesc': 'How much input do clients typically have in the therapeutic process? Can we discuss the frequency and format of sessions that would work best for me?', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': "Kevgiuqek'ngam Ilagaucaraa", 'yDesc': "Qaillun amllertalriamek ikayuutelartat kevgiuqek'ngat ikayungcaryaramun? Qalaruteksugngaarpuk-qaa quyurtellermegnuk amllertacirkaa ayuqucirkaa-llu assinrullerkaanun wangnun?", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ["Qaillunamllertalriamekikayuutelartatkevgiuqek'ngatikayungcaryaramun?Qalaruteksugngaarpuk-qaaquyurtellermegnukamllertacirkaaayuqucirkaa-lluassinrullerkaanunwangnun?"], 'resourceID': '10'}, '120': {'eTerm': 'Approach to Challenges', 'eDesc': "How do you handle challenges or conflicts in the therapeutic relationship? Can you provide an example of a challenging case you've worked on and the outcome?", 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Cakviurutet Auluksarait', 'yDesc': "Qaillun auluk'larciki cakviurutet wall' arenqiallugutet assiringcaryaramegni? Tangrruarutmek-qaa qalarcugngauten arenqialliuryaram caliaran tungiinun caliaqellerpenek qaillun-llu taqutellerpenek?", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ["Qaillunauluk'larcikicakviurutetwall’arenqiallugutetassiringcaryaramegni?Tangrruarutmek-qaaqalarcugngautenarenqialliuryaramcaliarantungiinuncaliaqellerpenekqaillun-llutaqutellerpenek?"], 'resourceID': '10'}, '121': {'eTerm': 'Termination and Closure', 'eDesc': 'How do you typically approach the termination or closure of therapy? What discussions or planning take place as therapy comes to an end?', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Iqukliciyaraq Qaqiucilleq-llu', 'yDesc': "Qaillun auluk'larcikek assiringcaryaraq iquklitarkaugaqan wall' qaqiuteqataraqan? Canek qalartelarcit wall' pillerkiurilarcit assiringcaryaraq iquklitniaraqan?", 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ["Qaillunauluk'larcikekassiringcaryaraqiquklitarkaugaqanwall’qaqiuteqataraqan?Canekqalartelarcitwall’pillerkiurilarcitassiringcaryaraqiquklitniaraqan?"], 'resourceID': '10'}, '122': {'eTerm': "<br>What's your name & date of birth?<br>", 'eDesc': 'Name and DOB are patient safety measures<br>Patients often have preferred names / nicknames that we write on the board / hand off during our report', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Kituuga atren, anutiiren-llu?', 'yDesc': '', 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': [], 'resourceID': '11'}, '123': {'eTerm': 'What name do you like to be called?', 'eDesc': 'Name and DOB are patient safety measures<br>Patients often have preferred names / nicknames that we write on the board / hand off during our report', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': '', 'yDesc': '', 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': [], 'resourceID': '11'}, '124': {'eTerm': 'What name do you like to be called?', 'eDesc': "Helps gauge orientation / how much they know of what's going on", 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Kituumek aciisqumasit?', 'yDesc': '', 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': [], 'resourceID': '11'}, '125': {'eTerm': 'If your heart were to stop, do you want us to do everything?', 'eDesc': 'Formally, this is called "code status" and refers to whether, if someone\'s heart stopped, we would do compressions / give emergency medications / intubate. Or, if they don\'t want those things, whether we change their "code status" in the chart to DNR / DNI - Do not resuscitate / Do not intubate. If someone wants a custom code status, this can be done too; it\'s up to them.', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Ircaqun aruliaqallikan, anirtuusqumauten-qaa? ', 'yDesc': 'Man\'a atengqertuq "code status-aamek", kangingqerrluni, kia ircaqua arulaiqan, negtaarluku ayagningnaqciqerput, anirtuutekaanek iirukiilluku, aneryaarcetaarluku cupluq iterrluku tuqluanun. Wall\', tuatnayunrilkata "code status-aarit" cimirluki chart-aitni DNR-aamun/DNI-aamun- Anirturyaqunaku/cupluliryaqunaku tuqluanun. Kina allamek piyukekngaminek code status-aaryukuni piyugngauq; ellaitnun at\'auq.', 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Man\'aatengqertuq"codestatus-aamek"', 'kangingqerrluni', 'kiaircaquaarulaiqan', 'negtaarlukuayagningnaqciqerput', 'anirtuutekaanekiirukiilluku', "aneryaarcetaarlukucupluqiterrlukutuqluanun.Wall'", 'tuatnayunrilkata"codestatus-aarit"cimirlukichart-aitniDNR-aamun/DNI-aamun-Anirturyaqunaku/cupluliryaqunakutuqluanun.Kinaallamekpiyukekngaminekcodestatus-aaryukunipiyugngauq;ellaitnunat\'auq.'], 'resourceID': '11'}, '126': {'eTerm': 'Do you have any allergies?', 'eDesc': 'Patient safety - very important for the chart', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Cam-qa puvqerrivkalaraaten? Tememun naulluqerrnarun, allergy-ngqertuten?', 'yDesc': '', 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': [], 'resourceID': '11'}, '127': {'eTerm': 'Are you having pain now? Where? How much does it hurt?', 'eDesc': 'Nursing is a practice of assessing & treating pain constantly', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Akngirquten-qaa (akngiaguten-qaa) watua?  Nauggun?  Qaillun pitalriamek akngirqessit? Enllugturiuten-qaa/Temiaguten-qaa? Nani? Qaillun pitalriamek enllugturcit?', 'yDesc': '', 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': [], 'resourceID': '11'}, '128': {'eTerm': 'Do you have chronic pain? Where? What do you take for it? What makes it worse or better?', 'eDesc': "Helps understand how much tolerance to pain meds they might have / what doses they're accustomed to, what meds / pain management strategies they might need to just maintain", 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': "Akngialartuten kessianek? Nauggun? Caaqavet utumarilarta? Cam arcarikanircetlartau wall' assirikanircelluku", 'yDesc': '', 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': [], 'resourceID': '11'}, '129': {'eTerm': "Hi I'm your nurse, my name is _______", 'eDesc': 'Do you need anything? <br>What do you need?', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Waqaa, Iinriurtekarpenga, atqa _______-aaruuq/auguq', 'yDesc': 'Cayugtuten-qaa? (This word can be used for both question.)', 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['Cayugtuten-qaa?(Thiswordcanbeusedforbothquestion.)'], 'resourceID': '12'}, '130': {'eTerm': 'How can I help you?', 'eDesc': 'Where is your pain? <br>How much does it hurt? <br>Would you like pain medication? <br>Would you like an ice pack or hot pack?', 'eNotes': 'Your next dose of pain medicine will be at...(time)', 'yTerm': 'Qaillun ikayuryugngasia?', 'yDesc': "Nauggun akngiasit? Qaill' pitalriamek akngirnarqa? Iinruyugtuten akngianritlerkan pitekluku? Qatugasuuteryugtuten-qaa kumlamek wall' puqlamek?", 'yNotes': "Akngianritlerkan pitekluku iinrunqignariiciquq ataam (sass'a-mi)", 'speakers': ["Nauggunakngiasit?Qaill'pitalriamekakngirnarqa?Iinruyugtutenakngianritlerkanpitekluku?Qatugasuuteryugtuten-qaakumlamekwall'puqlamek?"], 'resourceID': '12'}, '131': {'eTerm': 'Are you in pain?', 'eDesc': "I can't give you water<br>You're not allowed to eat or drink <br>What kind of juice do you want?", 'eNotes': "You're on a fluid restriction and can have (1 or 1.5 Liters) a day<br><br>Fluid restriction: The doctor orders a set amount of fluid intake by mouth per day for when someone has heart failure or renal issues. The nurse keeps track of everything liquid that the patient drinks (ie, coffee, water, juice, soup) & often has to negotiate with the patient about how much they've already had / what they want to drink and when, to stave off thirst but maintain within the allotted amounts", 'yTerm': 'Akngiaguten-qaa? Enllugturiuten-qaa?', 'yDesc': "Merkicescigatamken, Neresciigatuten wall' merciigatuten. Cakucimek juice-aryugcit?", 'yNotes': "Mell'erkan pillerkiurumauq waten-llu amllertalriamek (1 wall' 1.5 liters-aamek, gallon-am avganek wall' gallon-aaq muiryarpiarluku) ernermi meryugngaluten (Please show the patient 1 or 1.5 liters container)", 'speakers': ['Merkicescigatamken', "Neresciigatutenwall'merciigatuten.Cakucimekjuice-aryugcit?"], 'resourceID': '12'}, '132': {'eTerm': 'Do you want water?', 'eDesc': "We'll reposition you<br>Do you want to be repositioned?<br>Are you warm enough?<br>Would you like a blanket?<br>How is the temperature in the room?<br>Do you want pillows?<br>What can I do to make you comfortable?", 'eNotes': 'Is that better?', 'yTerm': 'Meqsugtuten-qaa?', 'yDesc': "Nugtakaninqigteqaataramteggen. Nugtakaninqigcesquten-qaa? Qerrutenrituten-qaa? Uligkicesquten-qaa? Puqlii mat'um cangaksiu? Putuskaryugtuten-qaa? Casqesia arenqilillerkarpet tungiinun?", 'yNotes': 'Assiriqertuq-qaa?', 'speakers': ["Nugtakaninqigteqaataramteggen.Nugtakaninqigcesquten-qaa?Qerrutenrituten-qaa?Uligkicesquten-qaa?Puqliimat'umcangaksiu?Putuskaryugtuten-qaa?Casqesiaarenqilillerkarpettungiinun?"], 'resourceID': '12'}, '133': {'eTerm': 'Are you comfortable?', 'eDesc': "We don't want you to fall<br>In the ICU, you need to have staff with you to walk<br>Your muscles are weak and you could hurt yourself if you try to get out of bed on your own<br>Physical Therapy will come work with you", 'eNotes': 'Do you want to go for a walk?<br>Do you want to sit in a chair?<br>I\'m going to grab a coworker and we\'ll help you<br>Do you want to get back in bed?<br>We can walk down the hallway together<br>Hold my hand<br>I\'ll help you<br>Wait for me<br>I\'ll be right back<br><br>Physical Therapy / PT: in ICU setting, comes during daytime primarily on weekdays; helps "mobilize" patients / the team helps figure out which assistive devices (canes, walker, etc) are most appropriate for people to get out of bed with. If someone has been sedated / unconscious for a while, we typically wait until PT comes to get them out of bed for the first time, if their muscles are deconditioned / if they haven\'t used their muscles in a while', 'yTerm': 'Arenqigtuten-qaa?', 'yDesc': 'Igcesqumanritamteggen. ICU-mi, calistemek malingqerrarkauguten piyuakuvet. Temevet yualui kayuitut maktengnaqkuvet-llu elpenek akngircuartuten. Kayungcaristem ullagluten kayungcaryarturceciiqaaten. ', 'yNotes': "Piyuaqeryugtuten-qaa?                  Aqumllermi-qaa aqumyugtuten?            Allamek calistemek ikayungcaqatartua. Inglerpenun-qaa atam inarcugtuten? Piyuanaurtukuk qagani maliklunuk. Tass'uqnga.                           Ikayurciqamken.                               Utaqalua.                                              Ataam taiciqua.", 'speakers': ['Igcesqumanritamteggen.ICU-mi', 'calistemekmalingqerrarkaugutenpiyuakuvet.Temevetyualuikayuitutmaktengnaqkuvet-lluelpenekakngircuartuten.Kayungcaristemullaglutenkayungcaryarturceciiqaaten.'], 'resourceID': '12'}, '134': {'eTerm': "You can't get out of bed", 'eDesc': '"Call don\'t fall" - a phrase in hospital rooms<br>You can call me for anything<br>We have time for you<br>We want to care for you, let us know what you need', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Inglerpenek atrarciigatuuten', 'yDesc': '"Qayagaurluten igcaqunak" iinrivigmi qaneryarauguq. Qayagauryugngaarpenga cayukuvet. Sass\'angqertukut elpenun. Auluksugamteggen, nallunrirceskikut cayukuvet.', 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': ['"Qayagaurlutenigcaqunak"iinrivigmiqaneryarauguq.Qayagauryugngaarpengacayukuvet.Sass\'angqertukutelpenun.Auluksugamteggen', 'nallunrirceskikutcayukuvet.'], 'resourceID': '12'}, '135': {'eTerm': "Here's your call bell if you need me", 'eDesc': "Do you need to poop or pee?<br>We're going to clean you up<br>We're going to help you onto a bedpan<br>You have a catheter that's taking away your urine<br>If you need to pee, call me<br>Here is your urinal<br>Can you turn in the bed by yourself? Or do you want our help?", 'eNotes': 'Turn away from me<br>Turn towards me<br>Grab onto the siderails<br>Put your hands across your chest<br>Give yourself a hug<br>Do you want music playing?<br>What kind of music do you like?<br><br>"Catheter: can refer to any medical device that goes into the patient (ie, IV catheter, foley catheter, central catheter...)<br>Foley catheter / urinary catheter: ""foley"" is a brand name that we shorthand to refer to ""urinary catheter;"" urinary catheter is a tube that goes into urethra, takes away pee directly from bladder"', 'yTerm': 'Waniwa ikayuryukuuvet nallunaircuun kulukunaq', 'yDesc': "Anaqsugtuten wall' yuqercugtuten? Eruqataramteggen. Ingelrem yuqervianun elliqataramteggen. Qurrsuuten qiluruangqertuq teq'urpet ayagtuursuutekaanek.  Yuqercukuuvet, qayagauqai.  Waniwa yuqervin.  Elpenek-qaa nugtarcugngauten inglerpeni?  Wall' ikayuusquten wankutnun? ", 'yNotes': "Tunuteqernga. Caulua. Teguluku tamana igcailkutaq/ayapervik. Unategken qatgarpenun ellilukek akiqliqevkarlukek. Elpenek qell'uten. Yuarutnek niicugyugtuten? Cakucit yuarutet assiksiki?                                                 ", 'speakers': ["Anaqsugtutenwall'yuqercugtuten?Eruqataramteggen.Ingelremyuqervianunelliqataramteggen.Qurrsuutenqiluruangqertuqteq'urpetayagtuursuutekaanek.Yuqercukuuvet", "qayagauqai.Waniwayuqervin.Elpenek-qaanugtarcugngauteninglerpeni?Wall'ikayuusqutenwankutnun?"], 'resourceID': '12'}, '136': {'eTerm': 'Do you need to go to the bathroom?', 'eDesc': '', 'eNotes': '', 'yTerm': 'Yuqervigcugtuten-qaa?', 'yDesc': '', 'yNotes': '', 'speakers': [], 'resourceID': '12'}, '137': {'eTerm': 'Sepsis', 'eDesc': 'Sepsis is like, how when you get hurt, and your body rushes a bunch of protective fluid to where the injury is. The blood vessels expand and the area gets swollen, so that your body can repair the area. Sepsis is when an infection triggers the impulse to protect the body and causes swelling everywhere - all of your blood vessels expand. It can get out of control fast. Blood pressure drops and your vital signs go out of wack, which, without treatment, can cause your kidneys, brain, and liver, to be deprived of essential blood flow. Without treatment, organ failure and death can occur.', 'eNotes': '<u>Science / Pathophysiology</u>:<br><br>Sepsis is characterized by an infection that enters the blood stream and causes vital sign changes, like: high temperature, low blood pressure, high heart rate, high respiratory rate / rapid breathing. It is usually also accompanied by abnormal lab findings, in particular high or very low white blood cell count. <br><br><u>Common Treatments / Care</u>:<br><br>There are protocols for sepsis, including:<br><br>-Draw Blood Cultures & other labs<br>-Secure IV access<br>-Give fluid IV<br>-Give antibiotics<br>-Treat abnormal vital signs (ie, if they\'re feverish, give tylenol / ice packs, get their blood pressure up, give oxygen if they\'re struggling to breathe)<br><br>If the person continues to get worse, treatment can include:<br>-Pressors<br><br><u>Relevant Definitions</u>:<br><br>"-IV: intravenous. A tiny tube that goes into the vein, that allows us to give medications and sometimes draw blood<br>-Antibiotics: medications that fight infections<br>-""Fluid"": specific formulas of saltwater that we give through IV\'s to treat lots of different kinds of medical issues / keep someone hydrated<br>-Pressors: Also called Vasopressors, refers to a class of drugs that squeezes the blood vessels so as to increase blood pressure. There are several medications in this category, but are generally just referred to as pressors outside of detailed communication between healthcare providers"', 'yTerm': '1. Kilinrem siissia augmun iterluni alingnarqellriaruluni tuquciyugngaluni puvqercirituli.                   2.  Naullutem ciissian puvqercetellra augem avayai.', 'yDesc': "Sepsis-aaq waten ayuquq,  akngirtaqaavet, temvet-llu mer'i quyurrluteng kitugingnaqluku akngiruuten.  Augem nutngassutai qerrurluteng avatii-llu puvqercelluku, temevet assiringcarniarai avatii. Kilinrem ayagniraqaku mamtengnaqluku tema puvivkarluku temii tamalkuan. Tamarmeng-llu  temem avayai puvqerrluteng. Arcarillra cukayugngauq. Augem-llu nutngaarallra aciqsigiluni. Qailluqerrluni-llu yuuciq, aulukumanrilkata, yungcaumanrilkuni tartuq, pateq, tenguk-llu nuqlitengciqut augmek. Yungcaumanrilkuneng, cakunglluut calinrirciqut tuqunaqluteng-llu.", 'yNotes': '<u>Science / Pathophysiology</u>:<br><br>Sepsis-aaq nallunairumauq naullutem ciissian itraqaku augem ayagyaraa cimircelluki-llu temem ayuqucia, ukutun: puqlii quyigluni, augem nutngaarallra aciqsigluni, ircaquq cukaluni, aneryaarturallra-llu quyigluni. Augillrit-llu assirpeknateng, augpet cayailkutai (white blood cells) quyigluteng wall\' aciqsigluteng. <br><br><u>Common Treatments / Care</u>:<br><br>Sepsis-aaq maligtaquarkangqertuq makunek: -Augillrakun paqluku auga  allanek-llu  -IV-rumaurluku. IV-rkun merkilluku, -Iinrukiiluku, -Yuungcarnarqellriit yuungcarluki (puqlaniqata, Tylenol-arkilluki, kumlamek atrartengnaqluku puqlii, augan nutngaurallra mayurtengnaqluku, aneryaarrsuucirluku anerniqkan) Arcariinaqan-llu yuungcallran ilaksuumaa -nanilicarluki temem avayai (pressors)<br><br><u>Relevant Definitions</u>:<br><br>"GCY: IV-q: Cuplucuar itercimalria taqermun. Cuplucuayaaq itercimalria taqermun, yuungcuatekicugngaluku iliini-llu augirluku.<br>Iinruut: Yuungcautet assiringnaqluki temem naullutai<br>“Mer\'ungalnguuq”: IV-kun itercukngakput taryulget mer\'et yuungcarluki ayuqenrilnguut naullutet/kina mer\'iucetengnaqevkenaku <br>Pressors-Nanilicarluki temem avayai, Vapopressor-aanek-llu acituluki, yuungcaun qungagiyugngalria temem augin avayainek quyigingnaqluku augem nutngaarallra. Qavciugut yuungcautet wani, taugaam pressor-aanek apraqluki yuungcarviit calistait qanaagaqaameng.”<br>"<br>', 'speakers': ['Sepsis-aaqwatenayuquq', 'akngirtaqaavet', "temvet-llumer'iquyurrlutengkitugingnaqlukuakngiruuten.Augemnutngassutaiqerrurlutengavatii-llupuvqercelluku", 'temevetassiringcarniaraiavatii.Kilinremayagniraqakumamtengnaqlukutemapuvivkarlukutemiitamalkuan.Tamarmeng-llutememavayaipuvqerrluteng.Arcarillracukayugngauq.Augem-llunutngaarallraaciqsigiluni.Qailluqerrluni-lluyuuciq', 'aulukumanrilkata', 'yungcaumanrilkunitartuq', 'pateq', 'tenguk-llunuqlitengciqutaugmek.Yungcaumanrilkuneng', 'cakunglluutcalinrirciquttuqunaqluteng-llu.'], 'resourceID': '13'}, '138': {'eTerm': 'Pneumonia', 'eDesc': "An infection of the lungs. It can interfere with oxygen getting into the blood and make it hard to breathe. It can cause organ failure if it either becomes a systemic infection (for ex, sepsis), or if oxygen is unable to get into the blood to the point that organs aren't getting oxygenated (for ex, COVID pneumonia). ", 'eNotes': '<u>Science / Pathophysiology</u>:<br><br>In pneumonia, the areas of the lung that typically allow air to enter the body and interface with the blood stream become filled with phlegm and/or fluid. Pneumonia causes shortness of breath, changes seen on X-ray imaging, cough, congestion, and potentially other vital sign changes / changes in the person\'s disposition (ie, fatigue / unresponsiveness / organ failure).<br><br><u>Common Treatments / Care</u>:<br><br>Oxygen<br>Antibiotics (IV or oral/pills)<br>Supportive Care<br>Intubation: in which the doctor puts a tube into someone\'s mouth & trachea, to create an airway through which we can control someone\'s breathing using an ambu-bag or ventilator. During this time the person will receive tube feeds for nutrition<br>Ventilator: a machine that controls breathing<br>If the person is unable to get off the vent / be extubated, then they might be trach\'d and peg\'d<br>Tracheostomy: a hole in the throat that gives direct access to trachea, so that someone\'s breaths can be delivered directly by medical professionals long term<br>Trach often goes with ""Peg"", or G-Tube / Gastrostomy tube, which is a tube into the stomach so the person can receive nutrition<br><br><u>Relevant Definitions</u>:<br><br>""Oral"": by mouth?? So if we\'re saying ""oral medication,"" we mean a medication that\'s taken by mouth, or like, in a different context, if we say ""oral hygeine,"" we mean the hygiene of the mouth<br>-Supportive Care: Really means anything we do that supports the specific situation of the body of the individual in front of us. Can mean: pain management, fluids, ventilators, pressors, etc<br>-Tube feeds: a liquid mixture that we put through a feeding pump so people can get calories<br>-Vent: same as ventilator<br>-Extubation: taking the breathing tube out<br>', 'yTerm': 'Patsaqaq', 'yDesc': "Pugtautem kumlaqertellra.  Iterciigalivkaryugngaluku oxygen-aaq augmun anerniqnarivkarluku. Cakunglluut calinrircecugngaluki naulluutngureskan (sepsis-aatun) wall' oxygen-aq iterciigalikan augmun cakunglluut-llu calisciigalivkarluki oxygen-ailata (COVID-aaggun, patsaqercaraq).", 'yNotes': '<u>Science / Pathophysiology</u>:<br><br>Patsaqeryaraq, pugtautmi aneryiallrem itetukiini augem avaiyai imaryangaaqata cali/wall\' imangaqaata. Patsaqeryaraq anerniqnarquq, tangernaqluni X-ray-kun, qusernaqluni, umcignaqluni, temem-llu ayuqucia cimiryugngaluni/ayuqucia ayunrirluni (ayunrirluni/ellairrluni/cakunglluut-llu calinrirluteng).<br><br><u>Common Treatments / Care</u>:<br><br>Oxygen-aaq, Iinrurkat/Yuungcautet (IV-kun wall\' qanratgun) -Assirillerkaanun auluksaraq -Cupluliryaraq: yungcaristem cupluliraqaku kina qanrakun tuqluakun-llu, aneryaallra assiriqercetaarluku engelciqtaarrsuutekun wall\' aneryaarrsuutem massiinaakun. Watnallrani yuk nerqelarciquq cuplukun. -Massiinakun aneryaarrsuun: Massiinakun auluku aneryaartullra. -Yuk aneryaarrsuutaicesciigalkan / cupluicesciigalkan-llu, ukineliyugngalukek-llu tuqluakun aneryaaryugngallerkaa pitekluku wall\' aqsaakun nerqessugngaarkauluku. -Tracheostomy: ukineq tuqluani aneryaarcecugngariluku yungcaristenun. -Trach (Ukineq tuqlumi) atuulartuq ilakluku "Peg", wall\' G-Tube-aq / Gastrostomy tube-aaq, aqsam ukinran cuplua, cupluuguq aqsamun yuk neryugnganiartuq.<br><br><u>Relevant Definitions</u>:<br><br>“Oral”-Qanrakun?? Qanqumta “Iinrukiilluku qanrakun,” qanertukut iinrurarkauluni qanmikun, wall\' waten, allauqerluku, qanqumta, “qanrem carriumallerkaa,” qanertukut carriumallerkaanun qanrem.<br>-Supportive Care: Assirillerkaanun Auluksaraq: Kangingqertuq calput tamalkuan ikayuringnaqellriaruluni temiin naulluutainun ciuqamteni uitalriamun. Waten ayuqsugngaluni:  akngiallri aulukengnaqluki, mer\'ngalngurteggun, aneryaarcetaarluku massiinatgun, nanilicallritgun temem avaiyain, allat-llu.<br>- <br>', 'speakers': ["Pugtautemkumlaqertellra.Iterciigalivkaryugngalukuoxygen-aaqaugmunanerniqnarivkarluku.Cakunglluutcalinrircecugngalukinaulluutngureskan(sepsis-aatun)wall'oxygen-aqiterciigalikanaugmuncakunglluut-llucalisciigalivkarlukioxygen-ailata(COVID-aaggun", 'patsaqercaraq).'], 'resourceID': '13'}, '139': {'eTerm': 'Renal Failure / Kidney Failure / Renal Disease', 'eDesc': "The kidneys get rid of water, so if they're not working, fluid backs up throughout the body. The person stops peeing. The extra burden of fluid can cause swelling everywhere (esp in sepsis) and the toxins and electrolytes that the kidneys normally get rid of stay in the body. So, labs can get super out of wack, and if the person doesn't get these things out of their body, they can die. We monitor electrolytes frequently in order to make sure the lab values don't get too wacky.", 'eNotes': '<u>Science / Pathophysiology</u>:<br><br>Can happen because of an acute event, like sepsis - the blood pressure is so low that the kidneys don\'t get blood flow, and stop working - or from chronic disease, like diabetes - the persistently elevated blood sugar damages the blood vessels<br><br><u>Common Treatments / Care</u>:<br><br>-Diuresis: an intervention to help kickstart the kidneys into working. Diuretics ("water pills") help get rid of fluid and, as fluid is pulled out of the body, electrolytes & other toxins go with it<br>-Dialysis<br><br><u>Relevant Definitions</u>:<br><br>-Diuresis: producing urine. Pills & IV medications can help produce urine<br>-Dialysis: a machine that mimics the function of the kidney. There are several kinds of dialysis, including hemodialysis, which people can do outpatient, generally 3 x a week, and can also do if there\'s an acute event & they\'re in the hospital (ie, overdose), and CRRT - a continuous form of dialysis that can only happen in the ICU. Dialysis is run by nurses and a nephrologist<br>', 'yTerm': 'Tartuq Calinrirluni/ Tartuq Calinrirluni/ Tartuum Naulluutii', 'yDesc': "Tartum mer' ayagciquralaaraa, tua-i-llu calinrilkunek mer'ungalnguut ayagviirrluteng tememi. Yuk-llu qurrsuirulluni. Mer'ungalnguut tememi puvivkaryugngaa tem'ii tamalkuan (arcarqerluku naullluutem siissia augmun itraqan-sepsis) cali  tuqunarqellriit yuunqegcessuucet-llu? (electrolytes) ayagcetetukait tartum uitaurluteng tememi. Augillrit ayuquciimegteggun ayuqenrirluteng, tamakut antenrilkatki yuum temiinek, tuquyugngaluni tauna. Kelluquralaraput kesianek electrolyte-ait augit paqtellrit ayuquciicetun uitatassiirturluki.", 'yNotes': '<u>Science / Pathophysiology</u>:<br><br>Piciurcugngaluni alingnariaqan, sepsis-aatun-augem nutngarturallra aciqsilartuq tartuq-llu aungesciiganani, caliyuirulluni-llu - wall\' naulluutmun, augem tequm-llu saarralalissiiyaallra - saarralalissiyaallrem navgutui augem avayai.<br><br><u>Common Treatments / Care</u>:<br><br>Diuresis-aaq: tequrkiurissiiyaagluni: ikayurilria ayagnircetaarluku tartuq. Diuretics ("water pills"-review later iinruut mer\'uluteng) ikayurilartuq anciluni mer\'ungalngurnek cali, tememek anuraallerkait mer\'et, electrolyte-at allat-llu tuqunarqellriit tuatnalartut.                              Dialysis-aaq tartum carrirciigalkainek anciluteng<br><br><u>Relevant Definitions</u>:<br><br>Diuresis-aaq: tequrkiuriluni. Yuungcautet IV-t-llu iinruit ikayuriyugngaut tequrkiuriluteng.                                          Dialysis-aaq: massiinam ayuqelitukii tartuq. Qavciugut dialysis-arcuutet, ilakluku hemodialysis-aaq, yuut aturyugngaluku yungcarvigmun itengqanrilengermeng, atu\'urpallulartuq 3 x nitilimi, cali atuugaqluni arcaqalriaruaqan  & yungcarvigmelngurnun ( ie iinrurturpallugaqaata), CRRT-qllu - dialysis-aarturcelluku ICU-melnguq.  Dialysis-aaq caliaqelaaraat iinriurcet tartuum yungcaristii-llu.<br>', 'speakers': ["Tartummer'ayagciquralaaraa", "tua-i-llucalinrilkunekmer'ungalnguutayagviirrlutengtememi.Yuk-lluqurrsuirulluni.Mer'ungalnguuttememipuvivkaryugngaatem'iitamalkuan(arcarqerlukunaullluutemsiissiaaugmunitraqan-sepsis)calituqunarqellriityuunqegcessuucet-llu?(electrolytes)ayagcetetukaittartumuitaurlutengtememi.Augillritayuquciimegteggunayuqenrirluteng", 'tamakutantenrilkatkiyuumtemiinek', 'tuquyugngalunitauna.Kelluquralaraputkesianekelectrolyte-aitaugitpaqtellritayuquciicetunuitatassiirturluki.'], 'resourceID': '13'}, '140': {'eTerm': 'Congestive Heart Failure (CHF)', 'eDesc': "Every time your heart beats, it pushes blood throughout your body. Heart failure is when the mucles of the heart aren't able to push hard enough to get blood through; this causes blood to back up. ", 'eNotes': "<u>Science / Pathophysiology</u>:<br><br>CHF is a chronic process over time & has significant impact on people's everyday lives, esp r/t fatigue, shortness of breath, and reduction in activity. People with CHF are often so tired and out of breath that it becomes hard for them to tolerate any kind of activity. When the heart isn't pumping fully, it can cause fluid to back up into the lungs (which is what causes shortness of breath) and/or legs, causing leg swelling. <br><br><u>Common Treatments / Care</u>:<br><br>-Diuresis, to get rid of the burden of fluid on the heart<br>-Fluid restriction<br>-Medications to help the heart pump stronger<br>-Supportive Care: meds to keep blood pressure in range, help out kidneys if they're having trouble, oxygen if lungs are struggling, etc<br><br>", 'yTerm': 'Ircaquq ellminek nutngaurarciigaliluni (CHF)', 'yDesc': 'Ircaqun nutngaaqami, augmek ayagceciilartuq temevnun.  Ircaqum nutngaurallra tukniarutngaqaami yualui ircaquum caknaanarituuq anciurallra augmek; waten-llu piaqami auk natvarviirutlartuq.', 'yNotes': "<u>Science / Pathophysiology</u>:<br><br>CHF-aaq akanun aturnarqellriaruuq  yuuciitnun-llu agtuumaluni, arcaqerluni r/t (review later) taqsuqercukaarluni, anerniqluni, cauratullri-llu ikegliluteng. Yuut CHF-alget mernurturalartut anerniquuraluteng-llu caurarciigaliluteng-llu. Iracaquq nutngaurallra tukniarutaqami, mer'ngalngurmek quyurcituuq pugtautegnun (tamana anerniqnaqlartuq cali/wall' iruk puvvlukek.<br><br><u>Common Treatments / Care</u>:<br><br>Diuresis-aaq, mer'ungalnguq augartuurluku ircaqumek.                                        -Qaillum amllertalriamek mer'kangqerrsaraq.                            -Iinruut ikayurluku ircaqum nutngaurallra tuknirivkarluku.                                   -Supportive Care-aaq: Iinruut ikayuriluteng augem nutngaarallranek ikayurluku tartuq arenqiallugtaqan, oxygen-arkilluku pugtautet cakviuraqaata, etc <br>", 'speakers': ['Ircaqunnutngaaqami', 'augmekayagceciilartuqtemevnun.Ircaqumnutngaurallratukniarutngaqaamiyualuiircaquumcaknaanarituuqanciurallraaugmek;waten-llupiaqamiauknatvarviirutlartuq.'], 'resourceID': '13'}, '141': {'eTerm': 'Withdrawal (Alcohol withdrawal, can also happen with street drugs, and can also happen because of the sedating medications we give in the ICU)', 'eDesc': "When someone's body isn't getting the substance it's used to, they can become very delirius and agitated. For alcohol, from day 3- day 10 without alcohol is the potentially life-threatening period. We treat their symptoms of withdrawal based on how severe symptoms are.", 'eNotes': "<u>Science / Pathophysiology</u>:<br><br>The receptors that alcohol & other drugs attached to are now free, which causes cravings and physical withdrawal symptoms. Most hospitals use a scale like this one to measure withdrawal symptoms. The higher the score, the more likely it is the person might have life-threatening symptoms, such as seizures. <br><br><u>Common Treatments / Care</u>:<br><br>We give medications based on the symptoms - so if someone is having very severe withdrawal, they might need so much sedation that they can't keep their mouth open / they're not awake enough to cough. But, if their withdrawal is mild, then we only have ot give them small doses, and they might be otherwise appropriate. Treatment for withdrawal is all considered supportive care; it really depends on the situation.", 'yTerm': "Aturturarraarluni camek atuyuirtellran ayuqucia temem elisngakiinek unangyuirucaaraam ayuqucia (revisit) (Taangarturatulim temii taanganritqallran ayuqucia temii taangamek atunrillran    iinrurrluut ilakluki, cali qavarcetaat/qinuirucetaat iinruitnek piicesciigacugngaluni, iinrukit'laqngamtenek ICU-mi)", 'yDesc': "Kia yuum temii unangenritaaqan camek elisngakiinek temiin, usviirtellriatun ayuqliriilartuq eqnayukaryuka'ariiluni-llu.  Taanganritaqami yuk 3-10 ernerni yuucimun alingnarqellriarulartuq.  Yungcalararput taqesciigalutai tangvagluki qaillun alingnarqucii. ", 'yNotes': "<u>Science / Pathophysiology</u>:<br><br>Taanganun iinrurrlugnun-llu qaillun pitalriamek picesciigalutait paqyutait akilirnaitut ma-i, Amlleret yungcarviit makucinek atulartut cuqtaqamegteki taqesciigatellrita ayuquciitnek.  Cuqtellrita naaqutait quyigaqaata, yuum tuquyugngallra alingutnarilartuq, qissarcugngaluni.  <br><br><u>Common Treatments / Care</u>:<br><br>Iinrukicilartukut ayuqucia tangvagluku - kina piicescigatlerminek piiteqallran ayuqucia temii qailluqerterpakan qavarcetaarnarqeciquq wall' qinuirucetaarnaqluni yaavet qanrit aitarcescigalillranun / tupagcigalameng-llu quserciganateng. Qailluqertellran-llu temii arcaqanrilkan, amllenrilngurmek iinrukiskuni, assirciqsugnarquq (ask Indra) Yuungcallra temem piitenritqallran qailluqercetallra supportive care-auguq; ayuqucianun tusngauq.<br><br>", 'speakers': ['Kiayuumtemiiunangenritaaqancamekelisngakiinektemiin', "u