let resourceIDs = {'1': [['Common Concerns about Seeking Mental Health Care', ''], ["Peng'garutai Yuallerkam Umyualiuryaraamek", ''], ['', ''], ['', '']], '2': [['Common Reasons for Seeking Behavioral Health Care', ''], ['Behavioral Health Care-aamun Ikayungcaryarat', ''], ['', ''], ['', '']], '3': [['Terms Related to Emotional States', ''], ['Aperyarat Umyuamun Tusngalriit', ''], ['', ''], ['', '']], '4': [['Terms Related to Cognition and Awareness', ''], ['Umyuartuyaaram Ellangqerrsaram-llu Aperyarai', ''], ['', ''], ['', '']], '5': [['Terms Related to Coping and Recovery', ''], ['Aperyarat Auluksaramun Utumariyaramun-llu', ''], ['', ''], ['', '']], '6': [['Social and Cultural Aspects', ''], ['Yuucim Yuuyaram-llu Ayuquciit', ''], ['', ''], ['', '']], '7': [['Treatment and Goals', ''], ['Yuungcaryaraq Egmirutekat-llu', ''], ['', ''], ['', '']], '8': [['Autonomy in Behavioral Health Care', ''], ['Ellminek Ataniuriyaraq Ayuqucim Calricaaraani', ''], ['Autonomy in healthcare is the principle that people have the right to make decisions about their own medical treatment and care. Autonomy means that providers must respect people’s rights and honor both their values and preferences. ', ''], ['Ellminek ataniuriyaaraq calricaarmi elluagiyaram kangiqaa yuut piunarqucingqerrniluki pillerkiurillerkaita tungiinun qaillun yuungcallerkameggnun auluklerkameggnun-llu.  Ellminek ataniuriyaraq kangingqertuq aulukestet qigcikarkaugait yuut piunarquciit cali qigcikluki arcaqakekngait qanruyutet piyullrit-llu.', '']], '9': [['Stages of Change', ''], ['Cimirturallret', ''], ["The Stages of Change describe the process a person goes through when making positive changes.                                                  It's important to note that individuals may not move through these stages linearly, and relapses are common. The model emphasizes the non-linear nature of change and the need for ongoing support and flexibility in the process. Additionally, not all individuals progress through every stage, and they may move back and forth between stages before achieving long-term success.                                       ", ''], ['Cimirturalleq qanrumauq yuk ayagturaraqami assitmun cimilartuq.                                                                                         Arcaqalriaruuq nallunritlerkaa yuut ayagturayuitellratnek kinguqlirquurluki assiriyaraat, cali ataam utermun assiirutenqigtelartut iliit. Tangruarutem qalarutkaa cimiryaraq kinguqliquuryaraunritniluku cali cingumayaraq ayagtuurnaqniluku ayagturallra-llu cimiqetaarnaqniluku. Ilaqerluku, yuut assiriyuitut ayuqluteng assiringnaqsarani, utertaaryugngaut-llu ayuqenrilngurnun assiringnaqsaranun assiripigpailegmeng.  ', '']], '10': [['Finding the Right Provider', ''], ['Yuallerkaq Assilriamek Umyualiurtekamek', ''], ['It takes courage to ask for help. Sometimes after taking that courageous step, people can feel unhappy or disappointed with their care and may believe that all providers will be the same. But there are many types of providers, many styles of support, and the patient should always have a provider that fits well and makes them feel comfortable. \nAsking the right questions when starting therapy is important to make sure that you and your therapist are a good fit and that your needs will be addressed effectively. \nRemember that your comfort and sense of connection with the therapist are essential. Feel free to ask any additional questions that will help you make an informed decision about whether this therapist is the right fit for you.', ''], ['Cacetuqutnguuq ikayungcallerkaq. Iliini ikayungcarraarluteng, yuut angnitelartut wall’ narrluklarait aulukesciulteng cali ukveksagucugngaluku tamarmeng umyualiurtet tuaten ayuqnayukluki. Taugaam umyualiurtetangqertuq ayuqenrilngurnek, ayuqenrilngurnek cingumastekanek, cali ikayungcalria umyualiurtengqerrarkauluni arenqilriamek uitanqegcinarqellriamek-llu.\nArcaqalriaruuq umyualiullerkarpet ayagnerani ellualrianek apqaurillerkaq arenqillerkarpetegnek umyualiurten-llu piyuuteten-llu elluarrluki qanaatekarkaullerpetegnek.                                                  Umyuaqluku uitanqegcillerkan assilillerkan-llu umyualiurtemun arcaqalriaruuq.  Nagutaunak apqauraqluten allanek apyutengqerraqavet ikayuutekarkavnek pillerkiurillerkavnun umyualiurta elluatukan elpenun.', '']], '11': [['Admission History', ''], ['Yuallerkat Apyutait', ''], ['Note: Nursing admission histories are done for every patient when they come in. Currently, if the patient does not speak English and there is no one available to interpret, we mark every field as "unable to assess" and the documentation is fairly incomplete. Admission assessments are opportunities to screen people for discharge needs & are designed to make sure that nothing falls through the cracks, so to speak. Here, I\'m listing the major questions we ask, and have a short explanation of why if it might not seem intuitive', ''], ['Cacetuqutnguuq ikayungcallerkaq. Iliini ikayungcarraarluteng, yuut angnitelartut wall’ narrluklarait aulukesciulteng cali ukveksagucugngaluku tamarmeng umyualiurtet tuaten ayuqnayukluki. Taugaam umyualiurtetangqertuq ayuqenrilngurnek, ayuqenrilngurnek cingumastekanek, cali ikayungcalria umyualiurtengqerrarkauluni arenqilriamek uitanqegcinarqellriamek-llu. Arcaqalriaruuq umyualiullerkarpet ayagnerani ellualrianek apqaurillerkaq arenqillerkarpetegnek umyualiurten-llu piyuuteten-llu elluarrluki qanaatekarkaullerpetegnek. Umyuaqluku uitanqegcillerkan assilillerkan-llu umyualiurtemun arcaqalriaruuq.  Nagutaunak apqauraqluten allanek apyutengqerraqavet ikayuutekarkavnek pillerkiurillerkavnun umyualiurta elluatukan elpenun.', '']], '12': [['Basic Care', ''], ['', ''], ['Note: Currently, interpretation primarily happens through medical staff or family members who speak the language of our patients; if no one on staff has that language knowledge, we use a series of hand gestures, visual communication boards like the one found here, and guessing', ''], ['', '']], '13': [['Common Diagnoses', ''], ['', ''], ["Note: In this sheet, you'll find diagnoses we see on a regular basis, how I'd explain it to someone with no medical knowledge, a little bit of information on the patho, & treatments / care that might need to be communicated to the patient.", ''], ['', '']]};
